*Updated Description (Final Decision):*
After reviewing the discussions and Rafael Lechugo’s feedback, the initial proposal to use the hideIf() on the header based on the selected *Field type* has been dropped. 

The final implementation consists of transforming the "Display format" label into a header, thus gaining the option to hide/expand the two fields that belong to this section ("Display template" and "Display when zero"), in addition, when the "Field type" dropdown is changed, the "Display format" header will remain displayed and only the "Display template" field in that section will be hidden, in addition to the fields that were already hidden in the "Number field settings" section.
